  "id": "hearing-protection",
  "term": "hearing protection",
  "definition": "Hearing protection is something worn during a loud procedure, such as an MRI scan, to reduce exposure to noise. In this context, it is used to help limit possible hearing damage and may also reduce stress responses.",
